---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const articleLD = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": "BirkyStudio vs CINC (2026 Comparison), a Quoted Lead Machine You Rent vs a Front Desk You Own",
  "description": "Honest head-to-head comparison of BirkyStudio vs CINC for real estate agents. CINC is a managed real estate lead generation and CRM platform with quote-only pricing, reported from $899 per month for a solo agent plus a mandatory ad budget and a 6 to 12 month agreement. BirkyStudio is a done-for-you AI operator that answers your phone and WhatsApp 24/7, follows up automatically, and hands you verified prospects you own. Real pricing, real reviews, no bias.",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": "Luna Jerney",
    "url": "https://birkystudio.com"
  },
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "Birky Studio",
    "url": "https://birkystudio.com",
    "logo": {
      "@type": "ImageObject",
      "url": "https://birkystudio.com/images/birky-logo.jpg"
    }
  },
  "datePublished": "2026-10-27",
  "dateModified": "2026-10-27"
});

const faqLD = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much does CINC cost?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "CINC does not publish its plan prices. On its own pricing page all four tiers, Solo, Ramp, Pro and Select, say Request Pricing, and CINC's FAQ answers the cost question with an invitation to contact the team. What is published are the add-ons: CINC AI starts at $200 a month and a dialer is 3 lines for $75 a month. Third party reporting is consistent that the platform starts around $899 a month for a solo agent and $1,299 to $1,500 a month for a team, with buyer leads included, plus a mandatory co-managed ad budget that typically starts near $500 a month. By contrast BirkyStudio publishes every price: The Base Agent is $1,297 solo (Notion CRM included), the Text Receptionist is $297, the Voice Receptionist is $550 plus Vapi usage of about $30 to $50 a month, and websites are $499, $999 or $1,999 one-time."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does CINC answer my phone or reply on WhatsApp?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No. CINC is a lead generation and CRM platform. It captures leads on an IDX website CINC builds and runs paid Google and Facebook ads to fill, then routes those leads into its CRM. It does not pick up an inbound phone call and it does not hold a WhatsApp conversation, and CINC AI is an add-on for AI assisted follow up inside the platform rather than a voice receptionist. BirkyStudio's Voice Receptionist is $550 one-time plus Vapi usage of about $30 to $50 a month and answers calls 24/7 in English and Spanish, and the WhatsApp Text Receptionist is $297 one-time."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does CINC require a long term contract?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "CINC is reported to require a minimum commitment of 6 months, and agreements commonly run 6 to 12 months or a full year. Industry reporting says the terms generally require paying out the remainder of the term rather than cancelling at will, so if you want out at month four you may owe the balance. CINC does not publish the term either, so it lives on the order form. BirkyStudio has no contract and no commitment: you pay once for a build, and there is a 30 day money back guarantee on it."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Are CINC's leads good?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "CINC's own reviews are the fairest answer, and they split sharply. Capterra rates it 4.1 out of 5 from 249 reviews, and happy users describe consistent volume and closed deals, with one long time customer writing that CINC is the main reason their commissions have almost tripled. The recurring complaint is lead quality. A reviewer who stayed more than two years wrote that the cost is significant and simply was not worth it, another said the leads are almost all duds while over $1300 a month left the business, and a one star reviewer said the phone numbers, emails and even the names were wrong. CINC's public reply to those reviews points out that paid search and paid social leads need training, fast calling and time to warm up, which is a fair description of how the channel works. BirkyStudio's answer is a verified, enriched, scored prospect list you own, $497 Starter or $997 Pro one-time, with no bots and no dead numbers."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does CINC include a website, and do I own it?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes, a branded IDX website with property search, saved searches and alerts is part of the CINC subscription, and it is genuinely one of the reasons teams buy. What you do not get is ownership. The site is hosted and managed by CINC, so the pages, the search experience and the SEO equity built on those URLs belong to the platform, and cancelling takes the site with it. BirkyStudio builds a website you own for $499 for a 1 to 3 page Starter site, $999 for a Professional 4 to 7 page bilingual site, or $1,999 for a Premium 10+ page site with a blog. The code is yours."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is BirkyStudio cheaper than CINC?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "On a realistic all in basis, yes, by a wide margin. Third party reporting puts a properly run solo CINC setup at $1,800 to $3,500 a month once the platform fee, the mandatory $500 a month ad budget and the usual add-ons are stacked, which is $21,600 to $42,000 in year one. BirkyStudio has no monthly platform fee at all: the Base Agent is $1,297 one-time with the Notion CRM included, the Voice Receptionist is $550 one-time plus about $30 to $50 a month in Vapi usage, and the only recurring line is optional care at $97 a month (Care and Maintenance) or $197 a month (Business AI Partner). Year one with the Base Agent and the care plan is about $2,461, and year two is only the care plan."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What happens to my leads and my website if I cancel CINC?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Contacts can usually be exported, though reviewers report that notes, tags and behavioural history do not come across cleanly, and because CINC does not sell the platform without its lead generation, cancelling also ends the lead flow. The bigger loss is the website: every neighbourhood page, blog post and landing page you built on a CINC site sits at a URL CINC controls, so when the subscription ends the pages go dark, the links pointing at them break, and any search traction those specific URLs earned has to be rebuilt at new addresses. BirkyStudio builds the site on your own account, and the prospect list is a file you keep, so both stay with you if you ever stop working with us."
      }
    }
  ]
});
---

<BaseLayout
  title="BirkyStudio vs CINC (2026 Comparison)"
  description="Honest 2026 comparison: CINC is a real estate lead platform with quote-only pricing, reported from $899/month plus a $500/month ad budget and a 6-month contract. BirkyStudio gives you prospects you own and answers your phone."
  image="/images/comparison/cinc.jpg"
  >
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={articleLD} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqLD} />

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section style="padding:100px 0 80px;position:relative;overflow:hidden">
    <div style="position:absolute;top:0;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;background:radial-gradient(circle at 20% 50%,rgba(255,45,149,0.15),transparent 50%),radial-gradient(circle at 80% 50%,rgba(255,45,149,0.1),transparent 50%);"></div>
    <div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 32px;position:relative;z-index:1;">
      <div style="display:inline-block;padding:8px 20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:100px;color:white;font-size:0.85rem;font-weight:500;margin-bottom:20px;">
        Updated October 2026 • Honest comparison
      </div>
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(1.8rem,4vw,3rem);font-weight:800;color:white;margin-bottom:20px;line-height:1.15;">
        BirkyStudio vs CINC<br>
        <span style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--bs-accent),var(--bs-accent));-webkit-background-clip:text;-webkit-text-fill-color:transparent;">A Quoted Lead Machine You Rent vs a Front Desk You Own</span>
      </h1>
      <p style="font-size:1.1rem;color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;max-width:700px;">
        CINC, short for Commissions Inc., is the platform high volume real estate teams talk about when they want leads rather than software. It builds you a branded IDX website, runs paid Google and Facebook ads to fill it, and routes the leads into a CRM with behavioural automation, and it bundles buyer leads into every plan. Two things are harder to find: the price, which is quote only on CINC's own site, and a way out, since agreements are reported to run 6 to 12 months with the balance owed if you leave early. BirkyStudio is a one-time build. We answer your phone and WhatsApp 24/7 in English and Spanish, follow up automatically, and hand you verified prospects plus a website whose code you own. Here is the honest breakdown, including the parts where CINC wins.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Main Content -->
  <section style="padding:80px 0">
    <div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 32px;">

      <!-- Quick Answer -->
      <div style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--bs-bg-raised),var(--bs-bg-raised));border-radius:16px;padding:32px;margin-bottom:64px;border:1px solid rgba(255,45,149,0.3);">
        <h2 style="color:white;font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:16px;">⚡ Quick Answer</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          <strong style="color:white;">Choose BirkyStudio if:</strong> You want to know what you are paying before you get on a call, you would rather own your website, your pages and your prospect list than rent them, and you need the phone and the WhatsApp answered by something other than you. You get an AI agent that replies in seconds in two languages, an AI receptionist on WhatsApp and voice, verified, enriched, scored prospects you keep forever, and a site built on your own account that stays live even if you stop working with us.<br><br>
          <strong style="color:white;">Choose CINC if:</strong> Paid advertising is how you want to meet strangers, you have a defined farm area, you can carry a $500 a month ad budget on top of the platform fee, and you have a team with somebody whose job is answering the phone fast. CINC's hyperlocal ad targeting, IDX website and team routing are real, and buyer leads are included in the price rather than sold on top. For an established team, that is a legitimate business.<br><br>
          <strong style="color:white;">The honest difference:</strong> CINC is a lead machine you rent, and you cannot read its price tag without a sales call. It does not answer your phone, it does not hold a WhatsApp conversation, and it does not sell you the software without the lead generation attached. BirkyStudio is an operator we build for you, priced once and published, doing the answering and the following up, on a website and a prospect list you own outright.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Article Image 1 -->
      <div style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:64px;">
        <img src="/images/comparison/cinc-article-1.jpg" alt="Wide view of a bright open plan real estate office with a team working at desks across the room and natural light through tall windows" style="width:100%;max-width:800px;border-radius:12px;height:auto;box-shadow:0 4px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);" loading="lazy">
      </div>

      <!-- Why Compare -->
      <h2 style="font-size:1.6rem;font-weight:700;color:white;margin-bottom:16px;">Why compare BirkyStudio and CINC?</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
        These two get compared because both promise the same outcome, more qualified conversations without hiring, and because they sit at opposite ends of one question: do you rent the machine or own it? CINC is an all in one real estate lead generation platform. Every plan includes a CRM with behavioural automation and lead scoring, a branded IDX website with property search, saved searches and alerts, landing pages, a Seller Suite, mobile apps, video messaging, mass messaging, database imports and integrations such as Zapier, BombBomb and the Mojo dialer. It runs managed Google and Facebook campaigns, including cash offer ads and Google Local Service Ads for seller leads, and it markets itself on hyperlocal targeting by neighbourhood, school district and property type. Its four tiers are Solo for 1 user, Ramp for up to 4, Pro for up to 49 and Select for 50 or more.
      </p>
      <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
        BirkyStudio takes the other route. Instead of renting you a platform to operate, we build an AI operator that does the front desk work for you. The Base Agent reads every website and WhatsApp enquiry, sorts it, saves it to a Notion CRM built for agents, answers it instantly, and follows up automatically in English and Spanish. Add the AI Receptionist and the phone is answered around the clock. Add a Verified Prospect List and you start with real, enriched, scored prospects you own, no bots and no dead numbers.
      </p>
      <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:40px;">
        The real difference is not features, it is the price tag, the contract and who does the work. CINC does not publish its plan prices, is reported to start around $899 a month for a solo agent, requires a co-managed ad budget that typically starts near $500 a month, and is reported to lock you in for 6 to 12 months. BirkyStudio publishes every price, has no contract at all, and delivers a one-time build that answers your leads and that you keep. That is what this page breaks down, honestly, including where CINC is the better buy.
      </p>

      <!-- Comparison Table -->
      <h2 id="comparison" style="font-size:1.6rem;font-weight:700;color:white;margin-bottom:24px;">BirkyStudio vs CINC, Side by Side</h2>
