        <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          This is not a fight BirkyStudio wins on MLS depth, IDX search or paid lead volume, and we are not going to pretend it is. <strong style="color:white;">CINC runs one of the most serious managed ad operations in real estate</strong>, bundles buyer leads into the price, builds teams a genuine IDX website, and carries a 4.1 out of 5 rating from 249 Capterra reviews with long tenured customers who would say the same. If paid advertising is your growth engine, you have a farm area and a real ad budget, buy it for that.
        </p>
        <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          But be clear about what it is not. You cannot see the price without a call. It is reported to start around $899 a month before a minimum $500 a month ad budget, on a 6 to 12 month agreement that can leave you owing the balance if you quit. It does not answer your phone or hold a WhatsApp conversation, and CINC AI is a $200 a month add-on rather than a front desk. The website and every page you build on it belong to the platform, and lead quality is the complaint that repeats most often in its own reviews. <strong style="color:white;">BirkyStudio is a different purchase.</strong> You are not renting a lead machine, you are buying the front desk. The AI answers your phone and WhatsApp 24/7 in two languages, follows up automatically, and hands you verified prospects you own, on a website whose code is yours, for a price you can read on the page before you talk to anyone.
        </p>
        <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:24px;">
          The cleanest way to see it: CINC is an advertising operation with a CRM attached, rented by the month. BirkyStudio is an operator that answers and a list you keep. For a team with an ad budget and callers who can work leads fast, the right answer may be both, CINC for bought volume and BirkyStudio for the conversation that happens when the lead actually calls.<br><br>
          <strong style="color:white;">Choose CINC if:</strong> you want bought leads, hyperlocal ad targeting and a team platform with routing and seats, and you accept a 6 to 12 month agreement and a mandatory ad budget as the cost of that.<br><br>
          <strong style="color:white;">Choose BirkyStudio if:</strong> you want the price published, the phone answered, the follow-up handled, verified prospects you own and a website that stays yours, without a monthly platform fee or a year-long commitment.
        </p>
